      },
      "message": "feat(post): wire_edm and sinker_edm machine kinds and the .mch edm section\n\nTwo declared-only machine kinds for the EDM family (#290 D1): wire\n(X/Y, U/V for taper) and sinker (Z). The .mch file gains an optional\n`edm` section - guide planes, max taper, wire diameters, AWT; orbit\npatterns with the control's word, max orbit radius, pickup - absent\nkeys not stated, garbled ones refusing the file, the law restated in\nis_sane for project files. No op family admits an EDM, and posting now\nre-checks every op's family against its own setup's machine, so an op\nmade on a mill no longer posts after its setup is remounted onto steel\nthat cannot run it. Empty wire/sinker templates ship (no vendor\nvalues), kept out of the picker until an EDM op exists.\n\nPinned by edm_machine (7 tests).\n\nFixes #530\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
