      "message": "feat(post): EDM condition table as user data in the .mch edm section\n\n`edm.conditions[]`: the control's condition id, a name, the spark gap\nper side, the wire diameter (wire) or electrode undersize (sinker), a\nrough/skim/finish role and notes - the geometry a toolpath needs, never\nthe generator physics. Ids are required and unique, lengths scale with\nthe file's unit, a garbled entry refuses the file by its id, and\nis_sane restates it for project files. Edm::condition(machine, id, need)\nis the door an EDM op calls at command creation: a missing condition or\nan unstated field it needs is refused by name. No conditions ship.\n\nPinned by edm_conditions (6 tests).\n\nFixes #531\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
